---
import { SECURITY_POLICY_URL, SECURITY_REPORT_URL } from '@lib/support';
---

<section class="border-t border-line" aria-labelledby="kinds-title">
  <div class="wrap py-16 md:py-24 grid lg:grid-cols-12 gap-10 lg:gap-12">
    <div class="lg:col-span-5">
      <h2 id="kinds-title" class="h2">
        Feedback, problems and account help are different requests.
      </h2>
      <p class="prose mt-5 max-w-[46ch]">
        Choose the one that fits when you write. It changes the questions we suggest, not where the request goes or how
        it is treated. Security reports take a separate, private route.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="lg:col-span-6 lg:col-start-7 rule-list">
      <div class="py-6">
        <h3 class="h3">Beta feedback</h3>
        <p class="prose mt-2 text-base">
          Trying the beta? Tell us what worked, what did not, and what you need. A missing feature or an awkward step is
          feedback, not a bug.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="py-6">
        <h3 class="h3">Report a problem</h3>
        <p class="prose mt-2 text-base">
          Something broke, showed an error, or did not do what the docs say. Steps, the issue key and the exact message
          help most.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="py-6">
        <h3 class="h3">Account help</h3>
        <p class="prose mt-2 text-base">
          Signing in, two-factor, reactivating a deactivated account, or erasing your personal data. Use the form or
          email, and never send a password, recovery code or access token.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="py-6">
        <h3 class="h3">Security vulnerabilities</h3>
        <p class="prose mt-2 text-base">
          Report them privately through GitHub: the repository’s <strong>Security</strong> tab, then{' '}
          <strong>Report a vulnerability</strong>. Do not use this form, a public issue or a pull request.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-3 flex flex-wrap gap-x-6 gap-y-2 text-sm">
          <a class="link" href={SECURITY_REPORT_URL} rel="noopener">
            Open the Security tab
            <span class="arr ext" aria-hidden="true">
              ↗
            </span>
          </a>
          <a class="link" href={SECURITY_POLICY_URL} rel="noopener">
            Security policy
            <span class="arr ext" aria-hidden="true">
              ↗
            </span>
          </a>
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
